; The oracle script's contract, and the Makefile's reading of it. The tests
; use stand-in compilers they write themselves, so they run on a host that
; has no Jasmin compiler and never ask a real machine.
;
; Both files are dependencies: jasminc.sh is what the tests run, and the
; Makefile is what turns the script's exit 2 into the `fail` line that keeps
; a typo'd JASMINC from skipping the parity gate.

(cram
 (deps jasminc.sh ../../Makefile))
